      "id": 1,
      "text": "Upland incorporated May 15 1906, previously called North Ontario as part of the growing San Bernardino County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upland%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally part of the Ontario Model Colony founded by the Chaffey brothers, Upland grew into a thriving agricultural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://main.sbcounty.gov/2025/11/13/san-bernardino-county-history-upland/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1887 the Atchison, Topeka, and Santa Fe railroad reached Upland, connecting it to the newly founded Magnolia Tract.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upland%2C_California",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Euclid Avenue once hosted a trolley line and was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2005.",
